---
description: Rules for the TypeScript API
globs: ["apps/api/**/*.ts", "packages/shared/**/*.ts"]
alwaysApply: false
---

- strict TypeScript, no any, no non-null assertions without a comment.
- Zod schemas live in packages/shared and are the single source of truth for request/response types.
- Controllers stay thin; logic in services; DB access in repositories.
- Every endpoint: auth check, validation, rate limit where public, structured error shape, test.
- Parameterized queries only. Never log secrets, tokens or message bodies.
- Migrations are forward-only and committed with the schema change.
